From 8f8730a94434ac365950579488295288124444db Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Agnya <manthram@Pradass-MacBook-Pro.local>
Date: Wed, 9 Sep 2026 21:55:41 +0530
Subject: [PATCH] Rebrand to HiBowan: colors, sitewide rename, and safety/legal
 copy fixes

Color system:
- Remap brand/accent/text/ui tokens in tailwind.config.ts and the CSS
  custom properties in index.css (light + dark) from the old green/salmon
  Ceylon Expand palette to the locked HiBowan tokens: coral-red #DB354E,
  ocean blue #3F8AB4, deep navy #173B4D, cream #F8F4EA, white.
- Remap legacy ceylon-green/blue/dark aliases to the same tokens so the
  ~370 existing component usages of those classes pick up the new palette
  without per-file changes. Also defined the ceylon-orange/red/yellow/
  brown/cream/sand aliases that were referenced in a few places but never
  actually defined (previously invisible/no-op classes).

Sitewide rename: "Ceylon Expand" -> "HiBowan", "CeylonX Tribes"/"Ceylon
Tribes" -> "HiBowan Tribes", theceylonx.com -> hibowan.com, @theceylonx ->
hibowan.srilanka (including social link hrefs in the footer), across all
~40 files that referenced the old name (page titles, meta/OG tags, footer,
About, legal pages, comments).

Known bug/copy fixes:
- Corrected emergency numbers on Safety Guidelines (was Police 110/Medical
  111/Fire 111; now Police 119/Ambulance 110/Fire 110).
- Fixed the "Invalid Date" bug on Member Since / Last Updated (and a few
  other unguarded date displays) by validating the parsed Date before
  formatting instead of only checking the raw value was truthy.
- Removed "(from Replit authentication)" / "Replit's trusted system" from
  Privacy Policy, replaced with the actual Google/Facebook sign-in flow.
- Removed the false "AI-powered" claim from the recommendations FAQ answer
  (confirmed no AI/ML dependency anywhere in the backend) and reworded to
  describe the real preference-matching logic.
- Rewrote the About page's opening paragraph, which described "a local
  wanting to share your favorite hidden spots" as an example organizer,
  contradicting the foreigner-to-foreigner model. Also softened a similar
  line on the landing page.
- Purged "verified"/"verification" language implying identity checks that
  don't exist, across Safety Guidelines, Terms of Service, Privacy Policy,
  and the FAQ/profile pages -- confirmed via the backend that the only
  real signals are email-address-present and Q&A activity, never phone or
  ID. Simplified the VerificationBadges component to only the two badge
  types the backend can actually award, and removed the generic "Verified"
  shield that showed for any user with an email.
- Tightened the ToS "may change with advance notice" pricing hedge to
  match the locked model (free for travelers, indefinitely).

Not included in this pass: the page-level layout/structure redesign
(Home, Browse Trips, Trip Detail, Calendar, Tribes) matching the
prototype, the real logo icon (still the placeholder mark), and the
sign-up flow -- those are separate, larger changes.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
